---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout page={pages.about}>
  <p>
    A compact API response. A spreadsheet that needs to become a test fixture. A
    timestamp in a log that means nothing at a glance. These are small tasks,
    but they interrupt real work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Data Formatter Pro brings twelve everyday developer utilities into a
    consistent workspace. Open a tool, try a sample, inspect the result, and
    carry on. There is no account to create and no conversion API to configure.
  </p>
  <div class="about-values">
    <div>
      <h2>Useful before everything</h2>
      <p>
        Each tool performs a real operation and includes the technical details
        needed to interpret its output.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Local by design</h2>
      <p>
        Core transformations run in the browser. The default site has no
        analytics or advertising scripts.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Clear about limits</h2>
      <p>
        A decoded token is not a verified token. A CSV is not a lossless JSON
        backup. The interface tells you where those distinctions matter.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>A comfortable workspace</h2>
      <p>
        Readable editors, keyboard access, light and dark themes, and layouts
        that work from a phone to a desktop.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2>Made for everyday development</h2>
  <p>
    The toolkit covers structured data, encoding, identifiers, regular
    expressions, time, schedules, and HTTP responses. It is useful for software
    developers, QA engineers, students, and anyone who works with technical
    data.
  </p>
  <p>
    Browser-based does not mean perfectly secure. Use sanitized development data
    whenever possible, and consider the trust and extensions of the browser you
    use. Read each tool’s limitations before relying on its output in
    production.
  </p>
  <a href="/tools" class="btn btn-primary">
    Explore all 12 tools →
  </a>
</DocumentLayout>
